"tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A bundle is re-pinned only when every legacy member digest matches: an overridden member is\nchecked against the cached bundle artifact, every other member against its installed directory.\nThe release digest is recomputed from the new member digests."},"1363":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-44","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A bundle history release is checked against its cached artifact in `.fastskill/bundles/`, or,\nwhen that is missing, against the bundle's Lock entry."},"1364":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-45","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"A legacy value whose content is not installed, or whose installed content no longer matches it, is\nleft as it is and reported with the reason. Run `fastskill project install` to restore the content,\nthen run `project repin` again."},"1365":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-46","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#what-it-rewrites","content":"Bundle artifacts are immutable, so the command does not rewrite them. It reports each artifact\nthat still declares legacy member digests (in `.fastskill/bundles/`, in the Lock, or in the\nmanifest's `[bundles]`). Rebuild each one with `fastskill bundle build`."},"1366":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-47","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#find-legacy-digests-in-ci","content":"`--check` reports what a re-pin would do and changes nothing. It exits non-zero while any legacy\nvalue remains, so a CI job fails until the records are re-pinned and committed."},"1367":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-48","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#machine-readable-output","content":"The result uses the lifecycle envelope shared by the other project commands: `scope`, `outcome`\n(`changed`, `unchanged`, or `blocked`), `dry_run`, and one `targets` entry per legacy value with its\n`record`, `file`, `current_revision` (the legacy value), `target_revision` (the current form, when it\ncan be re-pinned), `changes`, and `retained` reasons. `legacy_artifacts` and `diagnostics` list the\nbundle artifacts to rebuild."},"1368":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-49","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"Code"},"1369":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-50","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"Meaning"},"1370":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-51","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"`0`"},"1371":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-52","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"No legacy digest remains (after a re-pin, or none was found)"},"1372":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-53","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"`1`"},"1373":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-54","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"A legacy value remains: under `--check`, or an entry left as is, or a legacy bundle artifact"},"1374":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-55","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/repin-command#exit-codes","content":"`2`"},"1375":{"id":"/cli-reference/repin-command-56","page_id":"/cli-reference/repin-command","tags":[],"ty