rence/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#read-only-by-default","content":"When writes are disabled, a request to a write endpoint returns:"},"1695":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-30","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#read-only-by-default","content":"Run `fastskill server serve --enable-write` when you want to manage skills (install / update / remove) from\nthe web UI or API on your own machine."},"1696":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-31","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#security-model","content":"`fastskill server serve` is **not a security boundary**: it enforces no authentication of its own (no token\nendpoint; API routes require no `Authorization`/`x-api-key` header). It is designed to run\n**local-first** on your machine."},"1697":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-32","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#security-model","content":"If you expose the server on a shared or untrusted network, put an **authenticating reverse proxy or\nsidecar** in front of it and ensure the app port is not directly reachable — the proxy owns request\nauthentication. Combined with the read-only default, this means an exposed instance without\n`--enable-write` cannot be used to mutate state even before the proxy is considered."},"1698":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-33","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#api-base-path","content":"All application routes use the `/api/v1/…` namespace."},"1699":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-command-34","page_id":"/cli-reference/serve-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/serve-command#health-probes","content":"The server exposes two standard health endpoints immediately after startup:"},"1700":{"id":"/cli-reference/serve-com