se they\nare side-effecting (disk, network, embedding-API cost), not just because they are destructive. This\nis one switch: `--enable-write` enables all mutations at once. See the\n`server serve` reference."],[3489,"\"Later\" means the agent watches its skills folders and picks the skill up during the session.\nFastSkill registers session-start hooks where it has verified support (today Claude Code and\nGemini CLI); every other agent is kept up to date by the timer. Agents add hooks and folders\noften, so check the agent's current documentation before relying on a row."],[1220,"\"OPENAI_API_KEY environment variable not set\""],[1221,"\"Permission denied\" on database"],[2055,"\"Project-level init requires --skills-dir\""],[2054,"\"skill-project.toml already exists. Use --force to overwrite.\""],[2290,"(`parallel: 0` here just means \"unset\" in the table renderer — the runner still falls back to CPU core count.) A broken `checks.toml` fails validation immediately, e.g.:"],[1259,"**`--progress` / `--no-progress`**: Force the progress bar on, or suppress it and show only the final summary"],[3730,"**`auth_token` failing** — set `FASTSKILL_AUTH_TOKEN` (or `FASTSKILL_TOKEN`) if you use a private\nregistry."],[1295,"**`build-cache.json`** — the change-detection cache:"],[486,"**`cache clean`**: To reclaim disk space after finishing with skills from a source no longer\nin use, or as routine cleanup on a machine used for many short-lived projects."],[485,"**`cache info`**: Before a `clean`, to see what is actually taking up space, or when disk\nusage seems higher than expected."],[3729,"**`embedding_config` / `api_key` failing** — add `[tool.fastskill.embedding]` and set\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`; without them semantic search and reindex are disabled (they skip silently, they\ndon't error)."],[1291,"**`index.db`** — the vector index:"],[3369,"**`managed apply`** deploys the listed skills into each agent's user skills folder, removes the\nones it placed that are no longer listed, and moves blocked content into the quarantine. With\n`allowed = listed` and `exclusive_targets = true`, content in an agent folder that the state\ndoesn't allow is quarantined too."],[3728,"**`project_toml` failing** — run `fastskill project init` to create `skill-project.toml`."],[2312,"**`should_trigger` affects pass/fail.** The engine creates an implicit required `skill_invoked` check for each case, with `expected` equal to the CSV value. An explicit `skill_invoked` check that applies to the case replaces the implicit one; `eval validate` rejects a contradictory polarity. Therefore `false` tests non-consultation and `true` tests consultation, subject to the selected backend's observability."],[3371,"**`skill list --check`** fails on `managed-blocked` and `managed-not-allowed`."],[2285,"**`true`**"],[1304,"**100 skills**: \\~$0.001 (less than 1 cent)"],[938,"**A file source** reads the state from a path. The skill archives it lists are read from paths\nnext to it, or from absolute paths."],[2792,"**A new version is written only when a step is accepted**, so version numbers count\n*accepted steps*, not steps. Once any step has been rejected they no longer line up with\nstep indices: if step 0 is rejected and step 1 accepted, step 1's diff is\n`skill_v0000.md → skill_v0001.md`, not `v0001 → v0002`."],[971,"**A timer.** Enrolling, including the first apply that enrolls, installs a timer that applies\nshortly after login and then every hour, each time after a random wait of up to 10 minutes:\na systemd user timer on Linux, a launchd agent on macOS, and a scheduled task on Windows. No\nuser timer is installed when a machine-wide one is present. Set `FASTSKILL_MANAGED_TIMER=off`\nto install none, for example on a machine without a user service manager."],[3081,"**Access Control**: Registry access is controlled by authentication"],[2122,"**Add skills**: `fastskill skill add <skill-id>` (registry, Git, or local path)."],[675,"**Advisory judge rows.** A `judge:<name>` row for a judge that does not gate never moves a `check_rate`. It is reported by the `judge_score` metric that names the judge."],[939,"**An `https://` source** fetches the state from the URL, and each listed skill archive from\nits `https://` URL. Redirects to anything but `https://` are refused. The state can be at most\n8 MiB and each archive at most 512 MiB."],[1286,"**API Key Issues**: Check `OPENAI_API_KEY` environment variable"],[3082,"**Audit Trail**: Publishing history is maintained automatically"],[249,"**Authors**: init, validate, eval, and ship skills via the platform."],[2991,"**Automatic rebuilding keeps the index fresh.** After `skill add`, `project install`,\n`skill update`, or `skill remove`, FastSkill\nreindexes automatically (unless `auto_reindex = false` or `--no-reindex`, and only when an\nembedding provider is available), so `resolve` reflects the current skill set."],[252,"**Automation**: `project install --lock` and reproducible installs in CI."],[1303,"**Average skill**: \\~500 tokens"],[1486,"**Behavior**:"],[647,"**Benchmark**"],[3079,"**Blob Storage**: Artifacts are stored securely with checksum verification"],[2162,"**Case-based evals** with `fastskill eval` to test expected behavior against prompts and rubrics"],[2119,"**Cause**: `--yes` was used at a project root without a skills directory.\n**Solution**: add `--skills-dir <path>`, or drop `--yes` to be prompted."],[2118,"**Cause**: a `skill-project.toml` is already present.\n**Solution**: pass `--force` to overwrite it, or remove the file first."],[358,"**Cause**: Another `fastskill` command is currently running and has acquired an exclusive lock on the lock file."],[2121,"**Cause**: the current directory is not writable.\n**Solution**: fix permissions or run in a directory where you have write access."],[370,"**Cause**: The lock file was manually edited incorrectly, interrupted during write, or corrupted by a bug."],[383,"**Cause**: The system cannot determine the standard config directory for your platform."],[2120,"**Cause**: the version (from `--set-version` or `SKILL.md`) is not valid semver.\n**Solution**: use a semver string such as `1.0.0`."],[2116,"**Changing the embedding model invalidates your index.** Vectors from different\nmodels are not comparable — and often not even the same length. After switching\nmodels, run `fastskill index rebuild` before searching, or results will be meaningless."],[2521,"**Check environment readiness**"],[1593,"**Check name**: Ensure the repository name matches what you added."],[391,"**Check permissions**:"],[2065,"**Checks for an existing file**: refuses to overwrite `skill-project.toml` unless `--force` is given."],[2315,"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."],[2891,"**Checks TOML*&#x2A; — the grading rules that score each response. &#x2A;(Optional, but without it there is no real grading signal — see below.)*"],[2732,"**Checks**"],[3080,"**Checksum Verification**: All downloads include SHA256 checksums"],[3055,"**cksum**: SHA256 checksum of the ZIP artifact"],[2488,"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."],[247,"**CLI**: single entry point for installs, checks, search, and evals."],[3603,"**Clock skew.** A state whose `issued_at` is more than five minutes ahead of the local clock is\nrefused."],[3351,"**Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`.**"],[394,"**Commit project lock to git**:"],[1294,"**Content**: Metadata and embeddings used by semantic search"],[1297,"**Content**: Per-skill file hashes used to decide which skills changed since the last run"],[2062,"**Context detection**: `project init` detects whether you're in a skill directory or a project root:"],[3187,"**Converts to internal format** for processing by:"],[390,"**Create the directory manually**:"],[747,"**Creates File**: Writes `skill-project.toml` with basic structure and commented examples"],[2519,"**Cursor doesn't see a skill**"],[2099,"**Custom**: any path you pass via `--skills-dir` or the prompt"],[2098,"**Default**: `.claude/skills`"],[1257,"**Default**: Shows a live progress bar with completion percentage (when stdout is a TTY)"],[2287,"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."],[3054,"**deps**: Dependencies (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[738,"**Detects Context**: Determines if you're in a skill directory (with SKILL.md) or a project directory"],[250,"**Developers**: install, list, read, search for what agents load."],[895,"**Development Mode** (with `skill-project.toml`):"],[384,"**Diagnosis**:"],[2523,"**Direct skill discovery** — Cursor reads installed skills from the skills directory, no sync step"],[395,"**Don't commit global lock**:"],[397,"**Don't manually edit lock files** unless you understand the TOML schema"],[3059,"**download\\_url**: URL to download the ZIP artifact"],[2986,"**Embeddings power ranking when available.** With `OPENAI_API_KEY` set (and\n`[tool.fastskill.embedding]` configured), FastSkill ranks skills semantically using the embedding\nindex."],[2736,"**Epoch**"],[382,"**Error**: `Global config directory unavailable: ...`"],[357,"**Error**: `Lock file is held by another process: /path/to/skills.lock`"],[671,"**Errored trials.** A trial with outcome `error` still carries check results, because the checks ran, over an empty trace. Every negative expectation and every tool-call ceiling passed there vacuously, so folding them would report an outage as perfect restraint. They are dropped from every rate and counted separately."],[673,"**Estimated cost.** Only the vendor-reported figure is summed. When no trial reported one, the line reads \"not reported\" rather than `$0.00`."],[2953,"**Example `checks.toml`:**"],[2925,"**Example `suite.csv`** (has both `train` and `selection` rows, plus a held-out `test` row):"],[1973,"**Example output:**"],[475,"**Example output**:"],[1411,"**Example Output**:"],[1491,"**Example Output**:"],[1559,"**Example Output**:"],[1570,"**Example Output**:"],[3063,"**Example:**"],[1588,"**Example**:"],[3224,"**Example**: If skill-project.toml has `version = \"2.0.0\"` but SKILL.md has `version: \"1.0.0\"`, the marketplace.json will use `\"2.0.0\"`. Similarly, if skill-project.toml has `author = \"New Author\"`, it will override the author from SKILL.md. The `name` field always comes from SKILL.md frontmatter for display purposes, as it is not present in skill-project.toml."],[1516,"**Exit codes**:"],[3342,"**Expose read-only.** For a browsable UI or REST view over your skills, run `fastskill server serve`\n**without** `--enable-write`. Every mutation endpoint returns HTTP 403, so an exposed instance\ncannot install, update, delete, reindex, or refresh anything."],[739,"**Extracts Metadata**: If SKILL.md exists, extracts version, description, and author from YAML frontmatter"],[3056,"**features**: Feature flags (currently empty, reserved for future use)"],[1168,"**File permissions**: Ensure you have read/write permissions for skill directories."],[1296,"**Format**: JSON"],[1292,"**Format**: SQLite database"],[3344,"**Front an exposed port with an authenticating proxy.** `server serve` enforces no authentication of its\nown and is *not* a security boundary. If the port is reachable off your machine, put a reverse\nproxy or sidecar in front that owns authentication, and make sure the app port is not directly\nreachable. Binding a non-loopback address is fine and expected behind such a proxy."],[3505,"**Front it with an authenticating proxy if you expose it.** If the port is reachable on a shared\nor untrusted network, put a reverse proxy or sidecar in front that owns request authentication,\nand ensure the app port is not directly reachable. FastSkill will not police the bind address for\nyou, and binding a non-loopback address is the normal, expected configuration behind such a proxy."],[2660,"**Gate metric options** (per case, then averaged across the split — see\nSetup):"],[2734,"**Gate metric**"],[745,"**Generates Skill ID**: Uses the current directory name as the skill ID"],[3246,"**Git marketplace**: a Git repository with a marketplace document."],[3107,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[3111,"**Git sources**: `{repository_url}/marketplace.json` (via raw content API)"],[1466,"**git-marketplace**: Git repository with `marketplace.json` for skill discovery"],[356,"**Global lock**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock` (Linux/macOS) or `%APPDATA%\\fastskill\\global-skills.lock` (Windows)"],[1545,"**Grid**: Human-readable columnar layout with the same fields as table"],[3247,"**HTTP registry**: an HTTP index and downloadable skill artifacts."],[1471,"**http-registry**: HTTP-based registry with flat skill index"],[3038,"**ID** → Second directory level (the package name, must not contain slashes, e.g., \"web-scraper\")"],[2960,"**If you omit `checks` from `optimize.toml` entirely, there is no grading signal at all**: with zero checks configured, every case's result list is empty, and an empty list scores `1.0` under every `gate_metric` (vacuously — \"zero required checks passed\" is trivially true). In that configuration every candidate patch looks perfect, so the gate has nothing meaningful to accept or reject on. Always configure `checks` for a real run."],[3235,"**Include all metadata**: Provide tags, capabilities, and author information"],[2990,"**Incremental index rebuilding.** A change-detection cache (`.fastskill/build-cache.json`) lets\nFastSkill\nre-embed only what actually changed, so keeping the index current is cheap."],[2124,"**Index for search**: `fastskill index rebuild` (requires `OPENAI_API_KEY`)."],[2123,"**Install from the manifest**: `fastskill project install`."],[889,"**Installs Skills**: Stages and commits each overlapping dependency closure as one recovery unit"],[3370,"**Installs** are checked by digest before anything changes: `skill add`, `skill update`,\n`bundle add`, `bundle update`, `bundle override`, `project install` and restoring personal\noverrides, and the same through `server serve` and `mcp serve`. Blocked content is refused;\nwith `allowed = listed`, so is anything the state doesn't list."],[779,"**Invalid IDs:**"],[765,"**Invalid versions:**"],[3512,"**It runs without a shell**, from FastSkill's configuration directory, with a 30-second timeout,\nat most once per process for each repository. The token stays in memory; it is never written to\ndisk, logs or error messages."],[1546,"**JSON**: Machine-readable array with fields: id, scope, name, description, latest\\_version, published\\_at, and optionally versions array"],[674,"**Judge errors and excluded trials.** A trial whose judgment errored contributes nothing to a `judge_score` — not a zero — and is counted in `totals.judge_errors`. A trial a gated judge could not judge is counted in `totals.judge_excluded_trials`."],[649,"**Judges**"],[399,"**Keep FastSkill up to date** to get lock file improvements and bug fixes"],[3233,"**Keep it updated**: Regenerate `marketplace.json` when skills change"],[2987,"**Keyword fallback otherwise.** If no embedding provider is configured, semantic ranking silently\nskips and resolution falls back to keyword matching — the endpoint still returns results, it just\nranks them without embeddings."],[363,"**Kill the conflicting process**:"],[1301,"**Large repositories** (1000+ skills): 10-30 minutes"],[3058,"**links**: Reserved for future use"],[386,"**Linux/macOS**: `~/.config/fastskill/global-skills.lock`"],[883,"**Loads Dependencies**: Reads `[dependencies]` section from `skill-project.toml`"],[2514,"**Loads the full `SKILL.md`** for relevant skills to get instructions and parameters —\nthe same content `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` prints."],[3249,"**Local catalog**: skill content and catalog metadata on disk."],[2989,"**Local vector index.** Skill embeddings are stored in a local SQLite vector index (path set by\n`index_path` under `[tool.fastskill.embedding]`), so resolution queries run against on-disk vectors\nwith no external service call at query time."],[1478,"**local**: Local filesystem path"],[882,"**Locates Project File**: Finds `skill-project.toml` at project root or walks up directory tree"],[2513,"**Matches task requirements** against each skill's `description` frontmatter."],[2524,"**MCP access** — register the FastSkill MCP server for tool-based access inside Cursor"],[1300,"**Medium repositories** (100 skills): 2-5 minutes"],[3515,"**Missing credentials fail closed.** An unset `bearer` variable or a failing command is an error,\nnever an unauthenticated retry. `pat` keeps its existing behaviour."],[3052,"**name**: Skill identifier"],[1288,"**Network Issues**: Check internet connectivity"],[3347,"**Never commit plaintext tokens.** Keep them in your shell profile, CI secret store, or a secrets\nmanager. Commit `skill-project.toml`; keep the token value out of the repo."],[3602,"**No rollback.** FastSkill records the highest `issued_at` it has accepted and refuses any state\nissued earlier. Receiving the same state again is fine."],[3513,"**Non-interactive runs are flagged.** When standard input or standard error is not a terminal,\nthe command sees `FASTSKILL_INTERACTIVE=0` and must not prompt."],[672,"**Not-observable checks.** A check whose evidence the backend cannot produce records `passed: false` for older readers. It is excluded rather than counted as a failure."],[2638,"**Note on `aggregate_group_size` and `gate_trials`:** unlike the other numeric fields, these two\nare not checked by `fastskill`'s own config validation. A `0` value parses fine and passes\n`fastskill optimization run`'s validation step, then fails once the training loop starts, as\n`OPTIMIZE_TRAINING_FAILED: TEXTGRAD_INVALID_CONFIG: gate_trials must be > 0` (or the\nequivalent for `aggregate_group_size`) — confirmed by running the binary with `gate_trials = 0`."],[2800,"**Note:** `best_skill.md` is the highest-scoring skill document seen across all accepted\nsteps — not necessarily the final step. If the last few steps were rejected, it reflects the\nbest earlier checkpoint. A run where nothing was accepted exports the seed document, with\nthe optimizer's protected-region markers added."],[2872,"**Note:** Resume uses the config stored *inside* the run directory, not your original config file. This ensures the run is reproducible regardless of changes you may have made to the config since starting."],[3211,"**Note**: `skill-project.toml` provides metadata support (id, version, description, author, tags, capabilities, download\\_url). The `id` field is required and must not contain slashes. The `name` field is not used in skill-project.toml - skill names for display come from `SKILL.md` frontmatter only. All fields in skill-project.toml take priority over SKILL.md frontmatter."],[3115,"**Note**: FastSkill will automatically try the Claude Code standard location (`.claude-plugin/marketplace.json`) first, then fall back to the root location if not found. Both locations are supported."],[3204,"**Note**: The output file is automatically placed at `.claude-plugin/marketplace.json` (unless `--output` is specified)."],[3343,"**Only pass `--enable-write` when you mean it.** Enable writes for local skill management from the\nbrowser/API — ideally on `localhost` only. Do not combine `--enable-write` with an open,\nunfronted port."],[3511,"**Only user configuration may name a command.** It lives in `repositories.toml` in FastSkill's\nconfiguration directory. A `skill-project.toml` that names a command is refused, so a cloned\nrepository can never make FastSkill run a program."],[248,"**Optional `server serve`**: HTTP API and UI on your machine for browsing and integrations."],[2526,"**Optional semantic search** — `fastskill index rebuild` + `fastskill skill search --local` when an embedding provider is configured"],[3195,"**Options:**"],[967,"**Options** (every subcommand):"],[476,"**Options**:"],[480,"**Options**:"],[1413,"**Options**:"],[1494,"**Options**:"],[1536,"**Options**:"],[3078,"**Organization Structure**: Skills are organized by publishing organization"],[1408,"**Output Format**:"],[1543,"**Output Format**:"],[1564,"**Output Format**:\nDisplays a table of versions with:"],[1552,"**Output Format**:\nDisplays comprehensive skill information including:"],[235,"**Package manager and operational toolkit for AI agent skills.** fastskill enables discovery, installation, versioning, and deployment of skills at scale. It implements the same `SKILL.md` conventions used by Claude Code–compatible agents, and adds **manifests**, **lockfiles**, **self-contained team bundles**, **validation*&#x2A;, optional &#x2A;*`fastskill eval`** runs, and **search**. Modern agents read installed skills directly from the skills directory — no metadata-file sync step."],[1549,"**Parameters**:"],[1561,"**Parameters**:"],[3186,"**Parses Claude Code format** directly"],[1167,"**Path issue**: Ensure FastSkill is installed and in your PATH."],[1289,"**Permission Issues**: Ensure write access to skills directory"],[1277,"**Piped output**: No progress bar (falls 