ext successful apply: at login, hourly, and at every\nagent session start where a hook exists. A machine that is on and can sign in applies it within\nabout 70 minutes, and its agents drop the skill from their next session. A machine that stops\napplying keeps what it has, however long that lasts: off, offline, or waiting for a sign-in.\nExpiry limits how long FastSkill keeps allowing installs under an old state, not how long\ninstalled content stays. The report tells a source\nwhich machines haven't applied recently."],[1363,"A bundle history release is checked against its cached artifact in `.fastskill/bundles/`, or,\nwhen that is missing, against the bundle's Lock entry."],[1362,"A bundle is re-pinned only when every legacy member digest matches: an overridden member is\nchecked against the cached bundle artifact, every other member against its installed directory.\nThe release digest is recomputed from the new member digests."],[2401,"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."],[676,"A case whose every trial errored is named in the output, and a metric that matched nothing **fails the command** even under `--no-fail`: a mistyped case pattern would otherwise make a gate quietly disappear. Check results that no metric claims are named in a warning."],[2670,"A case with zero configured checks — or one where every check is `required = false` — scores\n`1.0` under all three metrics (vacuously). This is the same \"no signal without `checks`\" gap\ndescribed in Setup."],[3287,"A catalog lets you discover skills and add them by their canonical IDs. Each\nrepository is an entry in `[[tool.fastskill.repositories]]` in `skill-project.toml`.\nLower priority numbers are searched first. Explicit `--repository NAME` selection\navoids ambiguity when several catalogs offer the same ID."],[3626,"A composed Manifest's `[[tool.fastskill.repositories]]` join the consuming project's for\nresolution, so a shared `repository` origin finds the catalog its own Manifest names. A local\nrepository `path` is relative to the Manifest that declares it. When two Manifests define the same\nrepository name differently, installation stops and asks you to rename one; identical definitions\nare merged. `fastskill repo` commands list and edit only the project's own repositories."],[3634,"A content digest names the exact files of a skill directory and is written as\n`sha256-tree-v2:<hex>`. A lockfile from an earlier release may hold 64-character digests\nwithout that prefix; they are still verified, with a warning, and are replaced when fastskill\nnext rewrites that entry. fastskill releases before this format report a checksum mismatch on\nthe new form, so upgrade every machine and CI job that shares the lockfile."],[2731,"A CSV file of eval cases with `id`, `prompt`, and `should_trigger` columns"],[3593,"a digest is in `blocked` and also in `skills` or `also_allowed`"],[3596,"a digest isn't in the current content digest form; the older bare-hex form is never accepted\nhere, because two different trees could share it"],[3272,"A digest proves that selected content has not changed; it does not establish that\nthe instructions or scripts are safe. Review sources before making them available\nto agents. See the security model."],[3265,"A Git marketplace, local catalog, HTTP registry, or ZIP catalog"],[3263,"A Git origin with a branch or tag"],[3638,"A global FastSkill directory is not automatically an agent's discovery directory.\nConfirm the location your agent reads or access global skills through MCP.\nGlobal lock restoration does not require a project manifest."],[3666,"A group filter excluded the owning root."],[972,"A hook or timer that can't be installed is a warning in the apply's report, not a failure."],[589,"A judge is one native chat completion per trial — no agent, no tools