y name) must meet these requirements:"],[3653,"The skills directory contains the installed files an agent reads."],[3717,"The skills directory exists and is a directory"],[3563,"The skills to install. Each entry has an `id`, a `digest` and an `artifact`."],[933,"The source and the signing keys come only from two files, never from a project:"],[937,"The source is either a local file or an `https://` URL."],[3700,"The standard validator expects a lowercase name of 1–64 characters using letters,\ndigits, and single separating hyphens. The description must be nonempty and at most\n1024 characters. Name and description help an agent decide when to load the skill."],[2701,"The suite CSV has zero cases tagged `selection`. Exact message: `OPTIMIZE_NO_SELECTION_CASES: suite has zero cases tagged 'selection'`."],[2703,"The suite CSV has zero cases tagged `train` (e.g. every row is `selection`/`test`). See Setup for the exact message and the full split model."],[2892,"The suite is a CSV file with one row per eval case. Required columns:"],[2292,"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."],[566,"The summary reports what each run actually got (`isolation:` line in table output, `isolation` object in `summary.json`), and a failed case's scratch workspace is kept under `<run-dir>/workspaces/` for debugging. Pass `--no-isolation` to restore the old inherit-everything behaviour."],[3360,"The system file"],[3490,"The system file is machine-wide. Everything else is per user: the managed store, the machine id,\nthe cached state, the quarantine, the hooks and the timer. Each user enrolls and reports\nseparately."],[934,"the system file, deployed by device management: `/etc/fastskill/managed.toml` (Linux),\n`/Library/Application Support/FastSkill/managed.toml` (macOS) or\n`%ProgramData%\\FastSkill\\managed.toml` (Windows). It must be owned by the administrator and\nwritable by nobody else;"],[2981,"The task text to resolve against. Must not be empty (`RESOLVE_EMPTY_PROMPT`)."],[2882,"The three splits"],[3315,"The token is sent only to the origin (scheme, host and port) of `index_url`. A\ndownload on another origin gets no token and must carry its own authorization, such\nas a pre-signed URL. A redirect to another origin is followed without the token, and\na redirect from `https` to `http` is refused."],[3312,"The token is the first line of standard output with the trailing line ending\nremoved. Output over 16 KiB, an empty token, or a non-zero exit is an error. Errors\nname the program and its exit status, never the token."],[1126,"The tree contains 50 leaf commands. Root help shows the namespaces as a compact table of contents.\nRun `fastskill <namespace> --help` to discover that namespace, then run\n`fastskill <namespace> <action> --help` for arguments and examples. A bare skill ID is not a\ncommand; use `fastskill skill read <skill-id>`."],[3685,"The two `managed-` values appear only when this machine follows a verified managed state (see\n`fastskill managed`). They take precedence over every other\nvalue, `managed-blocked` first, and `skill list --check` fails on them even for a skill outside\nthe current selection."],[3711,"The two tools for debugging FastSkill are `fastskill cli doctor` — an environment/configuration health\ncheck — and the global `--verbose` / `-v` flag for detailed command output."],[935,"the user file, `managed.toml` in FastSkill's configuration folder."],[2901,"The user message sent to the target agent."],[2847,"The usual cause is a suite with no `train` rows, which `optimization run` now rejects up front\nwith `OPTIMIZE_NO_TRAIN_CASES` (see Setup). This warning is the\nbackstop for every other way a run can end up doing nothing — for example a loop\nconfiguration that yields no steps. Treat it as a failed run, not a successful one:\n`best_skill.md` is the seed document, unchanged."],[3740,"The way you